---
// About page. Address: /about/
// Tells visitors (and Google) who runs the site and how picks are made. This builds trust.
// TODO: rewrite the first section in your own words.
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, OWNER_NAME, SITE_NAME } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About | ${SITE_NAME}`}
  description={`Who runs ${SITE_NAME}, how products are ranked, and how the site earns money, explained plainly.`}
>
  <article class="guide">
    <h1>About {SITE_NAME}</h1>
    <p class="lead">Honest help choosing gadgets, made by a student for students.</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      Hi, I'm <strong>{OWNER_NAME}</strong>, a Computer Science student. I built {SITE_NAME} because
      shopping for a laptop meant dozens of open tabs, confusing spec sheets and reviews that only
      praised expensive models. I wanted a tool that asks what you actually need and shows the best
      fits, with honest reasons.
    </p>

    <h2>How picks are ranked</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You choose what matters: budget, specs, and preferences like battery life or weight.</li>
      <li>Products missing a "Must have" are removed. The rest are ranked by how well they fit your answers, not by price or commission.</li>
      <li>Every product shows what it does well <em>and</em> its downsides. Every product, expensive ones included, has at least one con.</li>
      <li>Reviews are based on each product's published specs and how they compare with the alternatives.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Prices</h2>
    <p>
      Prices are checked by hand, and each product shows the date it was last checked. Store prices change often,
      especially during sales, so always confirm the price on the store page before buying.
    </p>

    <h2>How the site earns money</h2>
    <p>
      Some "Buy" links are affiliate links. If you buy through them, the store pays us a small commission at no extra
      cost to you. That keeps the site free. It never changes the ranking: a cheaper product that fits you
      better will always rank higher.
    </p>

    <h2>Get in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Spotted a wrong price or spec, or want a product added? Email
      <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> or visit the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
